            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>AIr sealing the locationes we discussed will help save energy on heat loss. Specificall in the laundry room around the water heater and plumbing penetrations. </airSeal>
                <mainWalls>The walls on the main part of the house are quite good, the addition is 2x6 construction with R-20 insulation. If you are considering romiving the siding this could be upgraded and eligible for a Good Energy rebate. </mainWalls>
                <foundation>Adding insulation to the floor will have a small increase in energy savings and comfort. Adding a minimum of R-20 will be eligible for a Good Energy rebate. </foundation>
                <windows>Replacing the windows will help increase savings and comfort in the home. </windows>
                <HeatingSystem>Consider installing a Cold Climate Air Source Heat Pump. They are affordable and will save energy up to -30 Celcius. These are also eligible for a rebate.</HeatingSystem>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
